ARTEMIS AT EPHESUS / 以弗所亚底米神庙
30-second 1920s-inspired newsreel, 1920×1080 at 24fps, Mandarin narration.

USED IMAGES
1. Antonio Tempesta, Temple of Diana at Ephesus under construction, 1608; publisher Johannes Baptista Vrints I; Rijksmuseum object RP-P-H-OB-44.044. CC0, https://creativecommons.org/publicdomain/zero/1.0/ . Historic imaginative depiction, not a scientifically verified reconstruction and not camera footage of an intact ancient temple. Used around 2.4–7.2, 10.8–18.0 seconds (including date-card background).
Source: https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Tempel_van_Diana_in_Efeze_Septem_orbis_admiranda_(serietitel)_De_zeven_wereldwonderen_(serietitel),_RP-P-H-OB-44.044.jpg
2. Giovanni Battista Borra, Plan of the Temple of Artemis at Ephesus, 1750; Yale Center for British Art, B1977.14.926. CC0, https://creativecommons.org/publicdomain/zero/1.0/ . Historical plan, not a current measured reconstruction or a nineteenth-century excavation record. Used 7.2–10.8 and 18.0–22.8 seconds, explicitly dated.
Museum record: https://collections.britishart.yale.edu/catalog/tms:27007
Source: https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Giovanni_Battista_Borra_-_Plan_of_the_Temple_of_Artemis_at_Ephesus_-_B1977.14.926_-_Yale_Center_for_British_Art.jpg
